{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs34 KidoPalette Help\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 KidoPalette is a macOS app launcher. Register the apps you use, group them in tabs, and open the palette from a hot corner.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Getting started\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360\ls1\ilvl0\tx360 {\listtext\tab 1.\tab} Open the launcher (hot corner, Dock icon if shown, or {\b Window \u8594 ? Toggle Visibility} / \u8984 ?\u8679 ?L).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360\ls1\ilvl0\tx360 {\listtext\tab 2.\tab} Choose {\b Add App} and pick {\f1 \fs24 .app} bundles, or drag apps from Finder onto the launcher.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360\ls1\ilvl0\tx360 {\listtext\tab 3.\tab} Use tabs to group apps. Double-click a tab name to rename it.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Hot corner\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360\ls2\ilvl0\tx360 {\listtext\tab \bullet \tab} In {\b Settings}, choose the trigger corner and whether hot corners are enabled.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360\ls2\ilvl0\tx360 {\listtext\tab \bullet \tab} Optionally enable {\b Show Full Screen} so the launcher covers the display (including above the menu bar and Dock).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360\ls2\ilvl0\tx360 {\listtext\tab \bullet \tab} Move the pointer into the configured corner to show or hide the launcher.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Apps and tabs\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360\ls3\ilvl0\tx360 {\listtext\tab \bullet \tab} Click an icon to launch the app (the launcher hides afterward).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360\ls3\ilvl0\tx360 {\listtext\tab \bullet \tab} Drag icons to reorder them, or drop between icons to insert.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360\ls3\ilvl0\tx360 {\listtext\tab \bullet \tab} Drag Finder {\f1 \fs24 .app} items onto empty space after the last icon to append, or onto an insertion gap to insert there.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360\ls3\ilvl0\tx360 {\listtext\tab \bullet \tab} Use the context menu to move an app to another tab or remove it.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360\ls3\ilvl0\tx360 {\listtext\tab \bullet \tab} Add, rename, reorder, or delete tabs from the tab bar (at least one tab remains).\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Settings\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Open Settings from the menu bar ({\b KidoPalette \u8594 ? Settings\u8230 ?}) or the gear button in the launcher (useful when the Dock icon is hidden).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360\ls4\ilvl0\tx360 {\listtext\tab \bullet \tab} Hot corner on/off, corner choice, full-screen presentation\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360\ls4\ilvl0\tx360 {\listtext\tab \bullet \tab} Show in Dock\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 App Sandbox notes\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Official builds run under {\b App Sandbox}. Adding apps via the Open Panel or drag-and-drop grants access; KidoPalette stores security-scoped bookmarks so registered apps keep working after relaunch.\par}
